    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0147" n="139" xml:id="pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.321D1 Advisory Committee/64</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Canada</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 629</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-16">September 16, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State transmits, for the information of the Legation, a copy of
                    a telegram which is being sent to the American Ambassador to Brazil<anchor
                        n="19" xml:id="d101-f1"/> regarding the provision which is being made in the
                    cotton program of the United States for the exportation of cotton to Canada.</p>
                <p>The Legation is requested to communicate to the appropriate Canadian authorities
                    the substance of the first four paragraphs of the telegram.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
